The colors I gave (yes, that was my post from 6 years ago) are
equivalent to the standard EGA/VGA text mode colors one would get from
the MS-DOS version, which may differ from the colors you were getting
(presumably from an Xterm or equivalent).

Incidentally, the color values in that post are slightly incorrect -
replace 82 with 85 (0x55) and 165 with 170 (0xAA) and it should be
pretty much perfect. If dark blue (i.e. floating eyes) is still too
dark, you might want to turn up your monitor's contrast and/or
brightness a bit.

